Chapter: BadgeTone
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites UI chapter Theme
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter StatusBadge

 badge-widget bound a colour in all five arms and used it in none, so every
 badge in the tree rendered untinted. A BadgeStyle now carries the tone the
 constructor already knew when it chose the colour.

 The colours are the control. They are unchanged by this, and a tone derived
 from a colour rather than from the meaning would still make the tone rows
 pass while saying nothing, so both are printed side by side.

Section: Body

  row : Text, Integer, Integer -> Text
  row (what) (tone) (color) =
    "  " & what & " tone=" & tone-name tone & " color=" & show color

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "status, by meaning:"
    print-line-uni (row "backlog  " (badge-status-tone 0) (badge-status-color 0))
    print-line-uni (row "todo     " (badge-status-tone 1) (badge-status-color 1))
    print-line-uni (row "active   " (badge-status-tone 2) (badge-status-color 2))
    print-line-uni (row "done     " (badge-status-tone 4) (badge-status-color 4))
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "priority, by meaning:"
    print-line-uni (row "urgent   " (badge-priority-tone 0) (badge-priority-color 0))
    print-line-uni (row "high     " (badge-priority-tone 1) (badge-priority-color 1))
    print-line-uni (row "low      " (badge-priority-tone 3) (badge-priority-color 3))
    print-line-uni (row "none     " (badge-priority-tone 4) (badge-priority-color 4))
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "labels, by meaning:"
    print-line-uni (row "bug      " (badge-label-tone "bug") (badge-label-color "bug"))
    print-line-uni (row "docs     " (badge-label-tone "docs") (badge-label-color "docs"))
    print-line-uni (row "wontfix  " (badge-label-tone "wontfix") (badge-label-color "wontfix"))
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "the tone reaches the widget, which is the whole point:"
    print-line-uni ("  urgent bar   -> " & tone-name ((badge-widget "b" (badge-priority 0)).wn-tone))
    print-line-uni ("  done dot     -> " & tone-name ((badge-widget "b" (badge-status 4)).wn-tone))
    print-line-uni ("  bug pill     -> " & tone-name ((badge-widget "b" (badge-label "bug")).wn-tone))
    print-line-uni ("  crit severity-> " & tone-name ((badge-widget "b" (badge-severity "critical")).wn-tone))
    print-line-uni ("  completed    -> " & tone-name ((badge-widget "b" (badge-process-status "completed")).wn-tone))
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "and badge-tone reads the same value straight off the style:"
    print-line-uni ("  urgent=" & tone-name (badge-tone (badge-priority 0)) & " done=" & tone-name (badge-tone (badge-status 4)))
  end

